cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PLEAP: Productivity Lab Efficiency Analysis Program"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Changhee
    family-names: Kim
    email: ckim@inu.ac.kr
    affiliation: "Productivity Lab, Incheon National University, Incheon, Republic of Korea"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ProductivityLab/pleap"
url: "https://github.com/ProductivityLab/pleap"
abstract: >-
  PLEAP is an integrated desktop workbench for Data Envelopment Analysis.  It
  covers radial CCR and BCC models under either orientation, the smoothed
  homogeneous bootstrap with Kneip-Simar-Wilson bias correction, Malmquist
  productivity decomposition, Tobit, truncated and OLS second-stage regression,
  and parametric and non-parametric group comparisons, and it produces
  publication-ready figures and tables from the results.  Every estimator is
  validated against established reference software, and those comparisons are
  part of the automated test suite.
keywords:
  - data envelopment analysis
  - efficiency analysis
  - productivity
  - Malmquist index
  - bootstrap
  - Tobit regression
  - operations management
